oria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"soup, broth, sauce, gravy","termine_origine":"zema","catena":[{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"zema","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"ζέμα","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-vul","nome":"Vulgar Latin","termine":"","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"la-vul","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"It could be directly inherited from Latin zema (“saucepan”). However, it is more likely that the word is from Ancient Greek ζέμα (zéma, “decoction, something boiled or fermented; extract; essence”), through a Vulgar Latin intermediate *zema. The current meaning in Eastern Romance is closer to that o"},{"parola":"ștează","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"(usually wooden) rod or bar, especially those used to hold together or form a net","termine_origine":"schidia","catena":[{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"schidia","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"σχίδια","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Latin schidia, from Ancient Greek σχίδια (skhídia)."}]}